---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../styles/blog-article.css';

const pageTitle = 'Audio Sync Speed Reading: Eyes and Ears on One Stream | BriskRead';
const pageDescription =
  'Why dual-channel Audio Sync beats flash-only RSVP tools: speech locked to the visual word stream for stronger focus and fewer missed sentences.';
---

<Layout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription}>
  <article class="blog-article mt-8">
    <div class="container max-w-3xl">
      <div class="glass glass-article">
        <p class="section-label">Differentiation</p>
        <h1>Why Audio Sync beats flash-only speed readers</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Most free online RSVP tools only move pixels. <strong>Audio Sync</strong> on <a href="/">BriskRead</a> pairs text-to-speech with the same flash stream so vision and hearing reinforce each other.
        </p>

        <h2>The problem with visual-only flash</h2>
        <p>
          At high WPM, it is easy to “see” words without encoding them. You finish the article and cannot restate the argument. That is a focus problem, not a moral failing.
        </p>

        <h2>What dual-channel means</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Eyes track the RSVP (or related) visual presentation</li>
          <li>Ears hear the same stretch of text at a matched pace</li>
          <li>When one channel drifts, the other pulls attention back</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>When to use Audio Sync</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Medium difficulty nonfiction</li>
          <li>Long sessions where pure visual flash fatigues you</li>
          <li>Commuting-style focus while still looking at the screen</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Turn it off for quiet libraries, or when the device voice is poor — quality depends on system voices in Chrome/Edge.
        </p>

        <h2>How to try it in one minute</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Open <a href="/">briskread.com</a></li>
          <li>Click <strong>Hear a sample</strong> (or paste your own text)</li>
          <li>Confirm <strong>Audio Sync: On</strong> in the reader controls</li>
          <li>Adjust WPM until speech and flash feel locked</li>
        </ol>

        <div class="callout">
          <p>
            If you are comparing “best speed reading websites,” ask: do they only flash, or do they offer dual-channel sync? That single feature filters most clones.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="article-footer">
          <p>Related: <a href="/blog/best-online-speed-readers">Best online speed readers</a> · <a href="/blog/rsvp-reading-explained">RSVP explained</a> · <a href="/#features">All features</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
